UnitSwaps::ClSwapExactIn
├── when a user payer selects a proportional spend
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSpendMode
├── when the recipient is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidRecipient
└── given the recipient is valid
    ├── when the pool path is empty
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPath
    ├── when a pool is not registered
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPool for the pool
    ├── when a factory does not recognize the pool
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPool for the pool
    ├── when a pool reports an unsupported pool type
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPool for the pool
    └── given every pool is validated
        ├── when the input token does not belong to the pool
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidPath
        ├── when the resolved input exceeds the signed integer maximum
        │   └── it should revert with AmountOverflow
        ├── when another callback caller is already armed
        │   └── it should revert with CallbackNotCleared for the armed caller
        ├── when the pool returns without consuming its callback
        │   └── it should revert with CallbackNotCleared for the pool
        ├── when the pool reports a positive output delta
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidSwapDeltas
        ├── when the final output is below the minimum
        │   └── it should revert with TooLittleReceived
        └── given the final output meets the minimum
            ├── when the payer is the execution owner
            │   └── it should pay the first pool directly from the execution owner
            ├── when the payer is the execution address
            │   ├── it should track the input token for the closure sweep
            │   └── it should pay the first pool from custody
            ├── when the input token is token one
            │   └── it should swap toward token zero using the upper price boundary
            ├── when the path contains multiple pools
            │   └── it should forward each returned output amount through custody
            ├── when a user payer routes through multiple pools
            │   └── it should pay only the first pool from the execution owner
            ├── when the hop directions differ
            │   └── it should swap each hop toward its own output token
            ├── when the recipient is the execution address
            │   └── it should track and return the output at batch closure
            └── when the output equals the minimum
                └── it should complete at the exact bound
